# The bar tabs on Steps: each one is its bar's 16 steps as a 4 x 4 grid of dots, so the whole pattern shows at once. A hit
# is a lit dot, a rest a dim one, a step past the pattern's end no dot; the playhead is the brightest dot, the bar it is in
# has a bar of ink under its tab, the bar the cells show a white ring. tests/strip_check.py reads the frames this writes: a
# shot's name says what it shows (t<track>_b<bar viewed>[_p<step playing, 0-based>][_s<kit sound>][_l<loop from>-<to>]).
wait 300
expect trk 1
# T1, a kit: kick on every fourth step from the first, snare from the third, over two bars
pat 1 1 32
step 1 1 1 1
step 1 1 5 1
step 1 1 9 1
step 1 1 13 1
step 1 1 17 1
step 1 1 21 1
step 1 1 25 1
step 1 1 29 1
step 1 1 3 2
step 1 1 7 2
step 1 1 11 2
step 1 1 15 2
step 1 1 19 2
step 1 1 23 2
step 1 1 27 2
step 1 1 31 2
# T2: 64 steps; the first bar's first column, the second's top row and last step, the third's diagonal, the fourth's
# last row and first step
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
pat 2 1 64
step 2 1 1 48
step 2 1 5 48
step 2 1 9 48
step 2 1 13 48
step 2 1 17 48
step 2 1 18 48
step 2 1 19 48
step 2 1 20 48
step 2 1 32 48
step 2 1 33 48
step 2 1 38 48
step 2 1 43 48
step 2 1 48 48
step 2 1 49 48
step 2 1 61 48
step 2 1 62 48
step 2 1 63 48
step 2 1 64 48
# T3: 64 steps, a hit exactly where T2 has none
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 3
pat 3 1 64
step 3 1 2 48
step 3 1 3 48
step 3 1 4 48
step 3 1 6 48
step 3 1 7 48
step 3 1 8 48
step 3 1 10 48
step 3 1 11 48
step 3 1 12 48
step 3 1 14 48
step 3 1 15 48
step 3 1 16 48
step 3 1 21 48
step 3 1 22 48
step 3 1 23 48
step 3 1 24 48
step 3 1 25 48
step 3 1 26 48
step 3 1 27 48
step 3 1 28 48
step 3 1 29 48
step 3 1 30 48
step 3 1 31 48
step 3 1 34 48
step 3 1 35 48
step 3 1 36 48
step 3 1 37 48
step 3 1 39 48
step 3 1 40 48
step 3 1 41 48
step 3 1 42 48
step 3 1 44 48
step 3 1 45 48
step 3 1 46 48
step 3 1 47 48
step 3 1 50 48
step 3 1 51 48
step 3 1 52 48
step 3 1 53 48
step 3 1 54 48
step 3 1 55 48
step 3 1 56 48
step 3 1 57 48
step 3 1 58 48
step 3 1 59 48
step 3 1 60 48
# T4: 40 steps, with hits written past the end (steps 41 to 64) that no dot may show
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 4
pat 4 1 40
step 4 1 3 48
step 4 1 8 48
step 4 1 17 48
step 4 1 33 48
step 4 1 40 48
step 4 1 41 48
step 4 1 45 48
step 4 1 48 48
step 4 1 49 48
step 4 1 64 48
# the kit, then the sound shown changed with its black key
tap SEQ
expect page Steps
turn ALGO -3
expect trk 1
wait 100
shot t1_b0.png
tapkey b1
wait 100
shot t1_b0_s2.png
# T2: the ring moves with OCT, the playhead is on a rest of the second bar, then on the last step (a hit); stopped, neither
# the playhead nor the bar of ink is drawn
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
wait 100
shot t2_b0.png
tap OCT+
tap OCT+
wait 100
shot t2_b2.png
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
bars 1.3125
wait 30
expect step 2 20
shot t2_b2_p20.png
bars 2.6875
wait 30
expect step 2 63
shot t2_b2_p63.png
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
wait 100
shot t2_b2_stop.png
# T3 and T4
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 3
wait 100
shot t3_b2.png
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 4
wait 100
shot t4_b2.png
# T2 edited behind the screen's back (no key): a hit cleared in the first bar, one added, the pattern cut to 40 steps
turn ALGO -2
expect trk 2
step 2 1 13 0
step 2 1 2 48
wait 100
shot t2_b2_edit.png
pat 2 1 40
wait 100
shot t2_b2_cut.png
# and whole again with a loop over its last two bars: the hits outside it are thinner
pat 2 1 64
turn SELECT 1
expect page Bar
press SEQ
key b2 down
wait 60
key b3 down
wait 60
key b2 up
key b3 up
release SEQ
expect loop 2 33 64
turn SELECT -1
expect page Steps
wait 100
shot t2_b3_l33-64.png
